            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<h4><strong>1. The Hidden Impact of Indoor Air Quality</strong> </h4><p></p><p>Most of us spend nearly 90% of our time indoors — working, resting, and recharging — but indoor air can actually be up to five times more polluted than outdoor air. From cooking fumes and cleaning sprays to pet dander and seasonal allergens, invisible particles are constantly circulating through your home. </p><p>Over time, these pollutants can cause fatigue, brain fog, allergies, and poor sleep, making it harder to stay consistent with your wellness habits. You may be doing everything right — eating well, meditating, hydrating — yet still feeling drained because your air quality is holding you back. </p><p><em>💡 Wellness tip: The Blueair Blue Pure Max family uses advanced filtration technology to quietly remove airborne pollutants, allergens, and odors — so you can focus on feeling your best.</em> </p><p> </p><h4><strong>2. Stress and the Energy of Your Space</strong> </h4><p></p><p>Your environment carries energy — both literally and emotionally. Clutter, poor ventilation, and chemical VOCs (volatile organic compounds) from paints, furniture, or synthetic candles can all elevate stress hormones like cortisol. </p><p>Breathing cleaner air helps your body stay in a rest-and-recover state, rather than constantly fighting off environmental irritants. When your home feels lighter, your mood follows. </p><p> </p><p><em>💡 Wellness tip: Open a window each morning, swap synthetic scents for essential oils, and add an air purifier to refresh your space throughout the day. </em> </p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
